 "notes": "Cliopatria has no Northern Nigeria Protectorate row (the north is inside its Sokoto Caliphate row to 1904 and the British Africa aggregate). The north is drawn from twenty modern states, an approximation; the keyframes 1900-1902 show only the part the British held, which is the claim minus the caliphate (Cliopatria 1900 shape) and Bornu.\nNot settled: the Sokoto and Burmi dates of 1903 (the Sokoto Caliphate dossier by af-03 ends in March 1903 on its own page); the Anglo-French convention and the Anglo-German boundary that cut the caliphate's northern and eastern lands away (Adamawa); the protectorate's capital before Lokoja; and the Bornu conquest's detail (Rabih's state, dossier state-of-rabih-az-zubayr, held Bornu 1893-1900 and is not named on the page). The amalgamation of 1914 is carried on to colony-and-protectorate-of-nigeria.\nCounterparts: royal-niger-company (af-04 dossier), bornu-empire (Cliopatria row only, to 1894), sokoto-caliphate (af-03 dossier)."
